# Metadata retention design C1

Status: DESIGN ONLY — reviewable proposal; fresh independent design PASS required before implementation. Conditional same-Convex per-request USD amount authority is supported by the accepted public source interpretation. This proposal preserves that original number; it does not provide whole-invocation categories/attempt/finality proof. Actual money domain and ACTUAL_PROOFS remain EMPTY, amount-bearing observations still UNKNOWN/fullK/STOP. Embed remains unchanged UNKNOWN. No frozen source or original assertions/failures were edited.

## Source authority and exact mapping

Source packet manifest SHA25647e6cd5b0594c4e14839a9bfd343c9e427a7321953cf3626b26c8cc0ac1fb636 has9 rows. Fresh review report SHA256f113623b7ac61dad661f1f39bca02435848608dbdb37de6aeddf221cc33ed4f3, accepted by ROOT for source interpretation only4.75. Public get-convex/ai-budget commit509977282bce11cc1ba41b9ca31897eb43124da8 README581–584 supports provider>=0.2.0-alpha.1 real per-request dollar cost providerMetadata.convexGateway.cost including cached/reasoning. Client237–255 identifies authoritative finite nonnegative USD numbers;659–669/862–883 consume generate results;898–904/919–925 consume stream finish metadata. Its rounding, estimates, callback/meter APIs, dependency, budget architecture, Jev and services are not adopted.

Installed @convex-dev/ai-sdk-provider0.2.1 index.ts51–80 reads usage.cost and assigns that SAME JavaScript number to convexGateway.cost. It does not round, normalize currency, or derive cost from tokens. cost_details is separately passed by object reference. createGatewayProvider84–94 wires extractor into OpenAI-compatible adapter. @ai-sdk/openai-compatible chat mapper395–399 calls extractor with rawResponse for doGenerate;419 returns providerMetadata;421ff exposes rawResponse in response.body. doStream566–578 emits raw chunk first when includeRawChunks, processes validated rawValue, and701–724 constructs finish.providerMetadata from buildMetadata. The Convex stream extractor updates last usage on any truthy usage and builds metadata from it; last usage missing cost can therefore drop an earlier cost. The new correlation rule must not invent that missing final amount.

V4 generate-result32 and stream-part finish providerMetadata support SharedV4ProviderMetadata, which is only Record<string,JSONObject>; these types are not finite cost/category schemas. Embedding mapper178 merely passes response.providerMetadata; no concrete Convex embedding cost extraction is supported here.

Frozen observer.ts17 drops generate top-level providerMetadata;19 drops finish.providerMetadata. Those exact files remain historical frozen. Proposed implementation mapping: selector functions + event schema/reducer + canonical budget guard in a NEW reviewed source installation; capture/lifecycle parser recognizes exact new transcript version, closed proof nomination types explicitly distinguish retained amount source. No same-byte harness replacement.

## Exact proposed private projection

Define private SelectedProviderCost = exact own-data object:
{state:"missing"|"invalid"|"present", cost:number|null, reason:"none"|"missing"|"shape"|"number"|"bounds"}.
Present has finite nonnegative number, excludes -0, reason none; missing has null/missing; invalid has null and shape/number/bounds. No currency or categories are supplied by a raw field. Conditional USD semantic provenance is source interpretation, never a fabricated raw currency member. No costNanos, costDetails, upstream metadata, other namespace, generation ID, caller label or synthetic default is projected.

Generate selector: original result.providerMetadata → own convexGateway → own cost, only data descriptors, after existing exact source/method/context selection. Append providerCost to existing generate event.data exact keys {body,content,finish,usage,metadata,providerCost}. Stream selector: only actual native type finish part.providerMetadata same path; append providerCost to existing finish event.data exact keys {finish,usage,providerCost}. Other native event kinds retain existing data bytes and digest rules; no new event is appended. Embed keeps the exact existing selection and has no providerCost.

An absent/undefined/null parent or absent/undefined/null cost yields missing, never zero. Present cost0 is retained as0 with original categories[] and UNKNOWN money. Wrong parent kind, array, unsupported prototype, symbol/nonenumerable/accessor at inspected parents, negative/-0/NaN/Infinity/string/BigInt/object cost yields invalid. Invalid numeric values are not serialized into canonical data; their invalid state is retained. Oversized/ill-formed selected inputs fail the observation boundedly and yield UNKNOWN; no clipped evidence survives. Getter execution is forbidden: descriptor.value only, never x[k] or object spread on original provider objects.

Inspected parent nodes are original result/finish, providerMetadata and convexGateway only. Inspect all immediate own descriptors at these parents to enforce ordinary own-data keys, but do not recurse into or copy unselected namespaces/costDetails. Parent key counts and selected cost graph consume the existing combined4096-node/depth16 and180000-byte observation allowance; introduce no independent metadata budget. Track selector visits cumulatively in the same observation budget ledger before retaining any event, alongside canonical combined transcript validation. Descriptor reflection can allocate a key list before bound rejection, as existing JS reflection does; this is not a promise of constant memory for arbitrary hostile Proxy objects. Arbitrary Proxy traps are outside the accepted official native/Convex plain-data boundary, and no zero-trap guarantee is claimed. Reflection throws→invalid/UNKNOWN; no proxy/caller-produced result is an authorized provenance source.

Reject selected-parent cycles/alias to an ancestor, e.g. metadata===result or convexGateway===metadata. Snapshot selected scalar immediately and freeze newly built ordinary projection. Raw/body and selected existing fields are detached under the existing graph guard. Sharing in UNUSED costDetails is explicitly ignored: provider source intentionally aliases raw usage.cost_details into metadata.costDetails, so whole-result recursive canonicalization would incorrectly reject legitimate unused aliases. Shared references or mutation of retained selected graph remain rejected; no original object reference survives retention. Mutating original cost/parents after selection cannot change frozen projection/event/digest. Do not await between descriptor snapshots and detachment/canonicalization; source response is trusted ordinary data, not a caller concurrently mutating it. Repeated reads of a mutable source must not be used as provenance.

## Correlation procedure and output

Only classify retained-cost evidence as correlated after all existing method-specific raw/native correlation and shape checks pass, plus:
1. Generate raw response.body.usage.cost is an own-data finite nonnegative non--0 number and Object.is(rawNumber, projected.cost). Raw ID/model must be actual supplied valid identifiers; native response ID/model when present equals raw; native text/content/token/finish correspondence unchanged. Actual model compared verbatim, never inferred from requested factory ID.
2. Stream projected cost exists only on the single native finish, after raw finish and final text-end. All raw usage.cost occurrences among <=8 usage-bearing raw chunks agree by Object.is; a raw usage-only tail may complete cost before native finish. Native finish cost must Object.is equal the retained raw cost; no finish/cost/usage/content tail after native finish. Raw ID/model remain stable and native response metadata agrees. Adapter last-usage-without-cost omission is missing, not reuse of previous number.
3. Existing transcript ended abort/deadline/error or genuine full terminal handling is preserved. An absent finish creates no finish metadata. A synthetic flush without correlated raw terminal is not terminal authority, even if it carries cost. A genuine completed error following a validated full terminal cannot create extra cost; later usage/raw/finish still invalidates the prefix.
4. Mapped present/raw missing, raw present/mapped missing, mismatched cost, foreign coherent pair, ID/model conflict, bound violation or unsupported output cannot produce correlated amount. Mapped/raw numeric conflict is explicit contradiction and cannot overwrite genuinely independently established earlier immutable accounting; no new positive receipt exists here.

Retained means a conditional per-request amount was copied; correlated means the SAME adapter result/finish/raw lineage was checked. Neither means all logical-dispatch attempts are billed completely or terminal ledger finality. A stable actual model differing from requested is drift; private evidence can retain its number and actual model association, but no current proof covers it and delivery remains closed. Do not erase cost because private output is withheld; eventual qualified full charge conversion is independent of text/vector length.

Nomination must not repurpose current extraction raw-usage-cost-v1 or fill observedCategories. Propose NEW private extraction identifier convex-metadata-cost-correlated-v2 for source evidence only; exact schema {version:2,source:"convexGateway.cost",method:"generate"|"stream",cost:number,providerEventSequence:N,rawUsageEventSequences:N[],responseId:ID,actualModel:ID,transcriptDigest:H}. Arrays sorted unique, nonempty raw usage cost origins <=8; generate sequence0 and source sequence0. Source/context/dispatch binding remains the existing closed Context, not caller fields. No current money proof accepts this identifier; closed money resolver returns UNKNOWN without a separately accepted complete whole-invocation proof. No public nomination API/source choice/proof argument. Embed cannot construct it.

No new public metadata field or result leak: projection/full nomination exist only in owned private canonical transcript/evidence; public receipt shape and privacy policy stay governed. Existing raw-cost diagnostic fields remain as originally specified; mapped metadata is not dumped or independently exposed publicly. Missing/invalid projection may record generic private reason but never raw upstream errors/headers/reasoning/costDetails.

## Version, digest, capture and stage closure

Proposed transcript.version=2 for generate/stream selectors, exact event union as above. NEW transcript canonical bytes/digest reflect providerCost; do not relabel version1 bytes or reuse old receipt hashes. Embed may remain version1 on its method-specific unchanged path; parser dispatch is exact {method,version} and rejects mixed schemas. Version1 historical evidence remains immutable, yields existing EMPTY result, and cannot be upgraded by caller/refinement. Capture must rerun version2 selector projection validation and full observer/correlation from the retained exact detached raw/body/event transcript; derive nomination and amount provenance itself; compare exact context/dispatch/native/wire/ID/model/raw event links/source installation. Hash alone is not a billing attestation. Modified number/state/sequence/ID/model/dispatch/schema/source/digest rejects.

Same14 order/models/factories/options/native and wire request hashes, profile1536/U/M/K314310, one reader,512 events,180000 complete canonical bytes,4096 combined nodes/depth16,8 raw usage events,1 native finish remain governing. Metadata selector cost is counted within those budgets; no new fetch, callback, tee, paid/native request, ledger read or AI-budget helper. No new phase or deadline renewal.

C09/C10 raw prefix events are unchanged before finish; rawPartDigest remains digest of exact same raw event. New transcript.version changes transcript digest and hence future capability nomination content/source hashes. Existing P/S/M1/M2 domains/fields and source installation pins cannot silently stay asserted current: a reviewed NEW installation must pin new observer/capture/issuer/verifier closure together; stage verifier reruns the new parser with EMPTY resolver and exact firsteligible semantics. The closed official-only authority, both seals, fixed one1000ms original phase, final no-async-gap checks/direct RPC, owned late work, no public partial, immutableT/currentL and postpurge denial remain unchanged. No version1→2 historical stage replay migration or old key/manifest reuse is authorized. Purge deletes provider projection and raw backing along with owned private text/transcripts; hashed/stableT retained summaries cannot reconstruct metadata or authorize positive capture without backing.

## Acceptance matrix for subsequent independent review/implementation

| Control | Expected observable outcome |
|---|---|
| Generate/finish raw=.000001 mapped same original number | Present + correlated private number; accepted upper-neighbor outward microceil would be2micro; moneyUNKNOWN/fullK/STOP |
| Native zero/raw zero | Present0; no absent→0; categories[]; UNKNOWN/fullK |
| Missing parent/cost, raw-only, mapped-only | Missing or uncorrelated; no positive nomination/proof |
| Negative/-0/nonfinite/string/object/undefined | Invalid or missing as specified, no unsafe scalar retention; UNKNOWN |
| Selected accessor/symbol/prototype/ancestor alias | Getter0; reject selected graph, no leaked references/positive evidence |
| Unused costDetails shared with raw usage | Ignored unselected alias; selected numeric correlation can succeed |
| Original objects mutated after snapshot | Retained projection, event bytes and digest unchanged |
| Cost duplicate equal / conflicting / final missing | Equal occurrences stable; conflict contradiction; last metadata missing stays missing |
| Stream usage-only tail before finish / after finish | Before allowed within raw8 and exact correlation; after invalidates evidence |
| Empty text segment left open, synthetic flush, second finish | Existing rejection; no invented terminal/cost |
| ID/model/dispatch foreign pair or stable drift | Foreign denies; drift retained privately but UNKNOWN/no serving delivery |
| Combined budget exact / over | Exact allowed; any added metadata causing byte/node/depth/event/raw/finish overflow fails without clipping/second budget |
| Capture mutation of cost/state/source/schema/digest | Full deterministic revalidation denial, no accounting downgrade/reset |
| C09/C10 stage/replay/purge | Fresh new-install closed capability only; same raw prefix identities; old proofs immutable; purged backing cannot resurrect |
| Embed, cancelled before finish, rejected attempt absent | UNKNOWN; no cost0 or category inference |
| Late amount aboveK/$10, private output withheld | Current UNKNOWN unchanged; future supported amount must convert full uncapped, never output-dependent |

DUMMY selector-controls.mjs is a finite illustrative selector/correlation specification model using Node ordinary objects. It tests original numeric preservation, missing/invalid/getter/prototype/alias/mutation, raw/mapped conflict and unused costDetails sharing; it intentionally cannot test imported current production code, combined graph runtime wiring, stage/capture or whole-charge completeness. Those remain mandatory subsequent implementation outcome gates after independent design PASS.

## Evidence and boundaries

Command-specific original inputs/preimages are minimal current files and exact public source packet/review; no broad recursive historical copying. Raw receipts carry UTC/argv/cwd/stdout/stderr/exit and source-before/post. First directory listing/recorder bootstrap is explicitly NOT_CAPTURED. Source/manifest/review pins and9-row closure independently checked; source unchanged across reads. Own QA/scratch recursive seals include all actual nested preimages except each exact self manifest. Seal integrity is not semantic qualification.

No product/source/tests/config/current driver/old QA/frozen assertions/private actual key/environment/service/network/paid/Git/dependency/subagent action. Current actual categories/all-attempt/drift/finality/native gates/proof registry remain EMPTY. Original money diagnostic FAIL and original C2 failures remain untouched. ROOT must obtain fresh independent design judgment before any implementation, source installation or positive admission.

